<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Brühl (Rhineland)</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Brühl is a town in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhineland">Rhineland</a> between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cologne">Cologne</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bonn">Bonn</a>, in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-rhine-westphalia">North Rhine-Westphalia</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. The archbishop-elector Clemens August of Cologne, of the Wittelsbach family, built Augustusburg Palace and the hunting lodge of Falkenlust there from 1725. These masterpieces of German Rococo, with their gardens, are now a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO World Heritage Site</a>.</p></div>
